Clear the hardware intent when the decoder falls back to software.

Ported from PR #2133.  Fixes the row "webm | vp9 | vorbis | vaapi" of the
2026-08-09 test table: "video: Unsupported, audio also lost".

hwaccels_decode_get_format() ends by returning a software pixel format when
no hardware format could be set up -- a VAAPI device with no VP9 decode
entrypoint is the common case -- but leaves ctx->iavhwdevtype at
AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_VAAPI.  The filter graph is then still built for hardware
frames, graph configuration fails, and the whole subscription dies instead of
degrading to audio only.  Clear the intent at that point.

Scope note: this deliberately touches only the tail of the function, the
point where format selection has genuinely given up.  It must NOT be extended
to the early return added by PR #2117 at the top:

    // Guard: delay HW frames context init until dimensions known.
    // MPEG2 (and others) can call get_format() before sequence header
    if ((avctx->width <= 0 || avctx->height <= 0) && ...)
        return pix_fmts[i];          /* first non-hwaccel format */

That path also hands back a software format, but as a deferral, not a
surrender: get_format() is called again once the sequence header gives the
dimensions, and hwaccels_decode_setup_context() is written to be re-entered
("clean up required if you call decode twice" -- vaapi.c, qsv.c).  Clearing
iavhwdevtype there would permanently disable hardware decoding for every
codec that probes the format early.

This is NOT the fix for the VP9/VAAPI encoder failure -- that one is at
OPEN_ENCODER, not in the decoder.  This patch is about not losing the audio
stream when the video side gives up.

diff --git src/transcoding/transcode/hwaccels/hwaccels.c src/transcoding/transcode/hwaccels/hwaccels.c
index 51bb6c749..dc1da077b 100644
--- src/transcoding/transcode/hwaccels/hwaccels.c
+++ src/transcoding/transcode/hwaccels/hwaccels.c
@@ -213,6 +213,24 @@ hwaccels_decode_get_format(AVCodecContext *avctx,
             }
         }
     }
+    /* No hardware pixel format could be set up -- either the device is
+       unusable at runtime, or it simply cannot decode this codec (VP9 on a
+       VAAPI device that lacks a VP9 decode entrypoint is the common case).
+       A software format was selected instead, so drop the hardware intent:
+       otherwise the filter graph is still built for hardware frames, graph
+       configuration fails, and the whole subscription dies -- taking the
+       audio stream down with it instead of degrading to audio only. */
+    {
+        TVHContext *tvhctx = avctx->opaque;
+        if (tvhctx && tvhctx->iavhwdevtype != AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_NONE &&
+            (pix_fmt == AV_PIX_FMT_NONE ||
+             !((desc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(pix_fmt)) &&
+               (desc->flags & AV_PIX_FMT_FLAG_HWACCEL)))) {
+            tvhwarn(LS_TRANSCODE, "hwaccels: [%s] hardware decoding unavailable, "
+                    "falling back to software decoding", avctx->codec->name);
+            tvhctx->iavhwdevtype = AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_NONE;
+        }
+    }
     return pix_fmt;
 }
 
